{"key":"LedgerWindow","text":"## LedgerWindow\n\nThe **Ledger Window** is a pseudo-spreadsheet over `NOS_Implementations.md`, the\nchronological tape of every implementation in NOS: one line per feature, fix,\nadjustment, infrastructure change or docs pass. Four tabs read the same tape four\nways - as a grid, by system, as statistics, and as a playback.\n\n---\n\n@layout\nHeader | 0.50, 0.05 | Live totals: implementations, active days, systems touched, the date span and the tape's synced-through date.\nTabs | 0.14, 0.10 | Sheet, Systems, Stats and Timeline - four views of the same tape.\nToolbar | 0.50, 0.16 | Search, the system filter, the five colored type pills, Clear, and the visible-row count.\nColumn Headers | 0.50, 0.22 | Date, System, Type and Description. Click a header to sort by it; click again to reverse.\nGrid | 0.50, 0.60 | One row per tape entry. Hover for the full description, right-click for filter and copy actions.\n\n---\n\n### Sheet\n\n- **Search** - click the search box and type; rows filter live on description and system\n- **System filter** - opens a menu of every system with its entry count\n- **Type pills** - feature (green), fix (red), adjust (blue), infra (purple), docs (grey); click to toggle, several can be on at once\n- **Sorting** - click any column header; the arrow shows the direction\n- **Right-click a row** - filter to that system, day or type, copy the raw tape line, or play that day on the Timeline\n- **Clear** - drops every filter at once\n\n### What the five types mean\n\nEvery line on the tape is classified as exactly one of these. Hover any type pill in the\napp to see the same definitions.\n\n- **feature** - a capability that did not exist before\n- **fix** - corrects behavior that was broken or wrong\n- **adjust** - refines behavior that already worked: tuning, styling, wording, thresholds, layout\n- **infra** - plumbing with no direct user-visible change: build and deploy, the Cloudflare Worker, editor tooling, asset moves, internal data shapes, diagnostics instrumentation\n- **docs** - documentation and in-app help content\n\n### Systems\n\n- One collapsible section per system, ordered by **Busiest**, **A-Z** or **Most recent**\n- Each header shows the entry count, a bar colored by its type mix, per-type counts and the date range\n- Click a header to expand it and list that system's entries; **Sheet** opens the system in the Sheet tab\n\n### Stats\n\n- Headline tiles: implementations, active days, average per active day, systems touched, and the peak day\n- **Type mix** - counts, bars and percentages; click a row to filter the Sheet to that type\n- **Daily activity** - one stacked bar per active day. Hover for the breakdown, left-click to open that day in the Sheet, right-click to play it on the Timeline\n- **System rankings** - the busiest systems; click one to open it in the Sheet\n\n### Timeline\n\n- **Play** walks the tape forward one active day at a time; the strip fills in behind the playhead and the counters climb\n- Transport order is the standard one: rewind to first, step back, play/pause, step forward, fast forward to last\n- **speed** is a slider from 1 to 12 active days per second, with the resulting run time beside it. Active days are not equal sized, so a 143-entry day and a 1-entry day each take one tick\n- Drag the **slider** or click a bar in the strip to scrub to any day\n- The list underneath shows everything built on the selected day\n\n### Where the tape comes from\n\n- Loaded from GitHub `SavedData/NOS_Implementations.md`. Nothing is bundled into the app, so the Ledger always shows the current tape rather than whatever was true on build day\n- If it cannot be fetched you get an explanation and a **Retry** rather than stale data\n- In the Unity editor the tape publishes itself when it falls behind the canonical file, so the deployed\n  Ledger stays current without anyone remembering to do it; right-click the title bar and choose **Save** to force it\n- Right-click the title bar to Save or Export the tape\n\n### Shortcuts\n\n- Button-driven; no special keys.\n\n### Status: Beta\n### Purpose: OS\n\n---","screenshot":""}